## Lucide
https://lucide.dev — ISC License
Icon path data (`shapes`) is sourced from the Lucide icon set.

Generated icons (`generated-icons.ts`) are extracted from `lucide-static@1.31.0`
(pinned exact, no `^` — see package.json devDependencies and the header of
scripts/generate-lucide-icons.ts). Pinned exact on purpose: Lucide's geometry
changes between versions (new icons, retouched paths, renames), and
regenerating the catalog should be a deliberate act (manual version bump +
review), never a side effect of an unrelated `npm install`.

### Removed brand icons

`facebook`, `instagram`, `linkedin` and `twitter` were carried over from an
earlier hand-curated set and have been REMOVED from this catalog. They no
longer exist in Lucide's canonical icon set, with indications of a deliberate
removal over brand/trademark risk — they are corporate logos, not generic
iconography. Lucide's ISC license covers Lucide's own drawing; it does not
grant any third party's trademark rights over their logo.

They are not reintroduced without explicit license verification. Consumers who
need them can supply their own `AnimatedIconDef` via the `[iconDef]` input,
which accepts any icon definition — nothing about them needs to live in this
published package.

