## morphicons
https://github.com/guillermolg00/morphicons — MIT License
Copyright (c) 2026 Guillermo

The mathematical core of `glyphflow/morph` is vendored from morphicons
`src/core/` at v1.7.0: `parse.ts`, `normalize.ts`, `resample.ts`, `plan.ts`,
`interpolate.ts`, `serialize.ts`, `spring.ts` and `types.ts` (SVG path parsing,
cubic normalization, arc-length resampling, closed-form 2D Procrustes matching,
polar interpolation and the damped-spring solver).

Vendored, not depended on: the upstream package ships framework bindings and a
DOM layer that drive their own animation loop. glyphflow keeps the maths and,
by default, replaces that layer with discrete WAAPI keyframes, so the core is
copied in and carries its MIT notice in each file header. Upstream's `dom/`,
`react/`, `vue/`, `svelte/` and `adapters/` are NOT included verbatim.

An optional "live" render mode (`live-morph.ts`, opt-in via `<gf-icon-morph
live>`) is structurally INSPIRED by upstream's `src/dom/index.ts` — a
requestAnimationFrame scheduler driving the same spring over the same
`interpPolar` primitive, every frame. It is not a verbatim copy: it is
rewritten over glyphflow's own already-vendored `core/` primitives, without
upstream's multi-framework `PathEl` abstraction or its WeakMap-based caches.

The MIT permission notice reproduced in full: see LICENSE-morphicons.

